<div class="container page-body"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENCY MATTERS</p><h1>Useful links.<br><em>Clear disclosure.</em></h1></header><div class="prose narrow"><p>The Code Clouds is an independent technology publication. Learning resources support the writing; this is not an on-site course store.</p><h2>Ordinary resource links</h2><p>The official provider resources on the learning page are ordinary links unless explicitly marked otherwise. A link does not mean the provider sponsors this site or endorses its content.</p><h2>Affiliate links</h2><p>If a link can earn us a commission when you buy, its offer card is labelled “Affiliate link” next to the link. Check the provider’s pricing, regional availability, refund terms, and final checkout details before purchasing.</p><h2>Sponsored placements</h2><p>If a placement is paid for, the card is labelled “Sponsored placement.” A discount alone is not evidence that a resource is useful or suitable for you.</p><h2>Offers and expiry</h2><p>Offer listings include a checked date, explicit expiry, and any supplied restrictions. Providers can change or withdraw offers. We do not invent coupons or promise that a listed offer is the lowest available price.</p><h2>Editorial boundaries</h2><p>Any future monetization must remain compatible with <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/github-pages-limits">GitHub Pages usage limits</a>. Those limits restrict sites primarily directed at commercial transactions. This site stays focused on educational writing, not checkout or paid account services.</p><h2>Suggest a correction or an offer</h2><p>Share the official provider URL, complete terms, and expiry with <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ravindra on LinkedIn</a>. A suggestion does not guarantee publication.</p></div></div>
